Minutes of the meeting of the eighth, kept as they occurred.

Seed: 4417802.
Present: four voices, drone rank, tuba, the little bell.
Order: opening drone; hymn in the fasola manner; stillness; second
hymn, the same tune inverted at the fourth; doxology; benediction.

The stillness ran long — near two minutes by the press-room clock —
and no one moved to end it, which the clerk records without complaint.

One oddity. At the doxology the tuba fired its raspberry amen, a figure
which the rules permit at a probability I had understood to be very
small. It landed on the word "Amen" exactly. Some in the congregation
took it for an error. The clerk did not, and notes that a printed thing
is allowed one blot if the blot is punctual.

No further business. The lamps were left burning for the Operator.

--
Holiness to the Lord — and a plain seat for the plain singer
